  "crossCuttingFindings": [
    "Early-family frontier steps at TL2, TL5, and TL8 intentionally exchange damaged-state resilience for higher operational capability; maturation at TL3 and TL6 restores resilience/Space efficiency without another peak-output increase.",
    "The TL9 Total Matter Conversion candidate is a deliberate pinnacle jump. Standard representative demand is rarely power-starved, but branch-heavy legal designs still exceed one-reactor output by 14 TP at the maximum stress point.",
    "Two-current-reactor installations become much easier to fit from TL6 onward because the entire ship miniaturizes and Hull capacity grows. This must be retested after AUX/mission components receive numerical Space/Power values; it is not evidence by itself that Reactor output should be reduced.",
    "Safe +1 TP Reactor overload reduces one-point shortfalls but does not eliminate sustained power tradeoffs because Strain limits only two safe uses in a 20-turn encounter model.",
    "Energy-storage branches are deliberately excluded from this first pass because storage changes inter-turn allocation rather than sustained generation and should be calibrated after the sustained-generation baseline is understood."
  ],
  "revalidationTriggers": [
    "Any change to primary Reactor Space or Operational/Degraded/Emergency TP.",
    "Material changes to Hull capacity or standard component Space across TL1-TL9.",
    "Material changes to Energy weapon, Sensor/EW, Shield recharge, PDS, or STL overload Tactical Power demand.",
    "Promotion of numerical AUX/mission-system Space or Tactical Power costs that materially compete with second-Reactor installations.",
    "Implementation or retuning of Energy Storage, auxiliary generation, or Reactor overload/Strain mechanics."
  ]
